{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1122389-looking-for-ogam-write-ups-can-anyone-help","id":1122389,"title":"Looking for Ogam Write-Ups, Can Anyone Help?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-29T10:37:40-07:00","id":1122389,"title":"Looking for Ogam Write-Ups, Can Anyone Help?","content":"Hi everybody, I am looking for some help in tracking down fanmade write-ups of a purview for Ogam. I know it doesn't play an overly large role in Irish myth, but I feel that at least it should be an option for people playing scions of Ogma, Dagda, and Lugh. I feel it should also be available somehow for a Tuatha character who desires to specialize in secret knowledge, mystic endeavors, relic creation, etc. I know it was mentioned in the fiction preview depicting the Dagda's library, but I feel historically that it was more than just a writing system considering the fact it was seeming only used for grave inscriptions, and the like in archeological evidence. Additionally if you recall its mention in myth, Ogma's message to Lugh (warning of an attempt to steal one of his wives) simply consisted of the symbol Beith used four times and not an actual word or sentence. I have studied Irish Reconstructionist Pagan writings on the subject (I personally recommend Erynn Rowan Laurie's &quot;Ogam: Weaving Word Wisdom&quot;) and they indicate it was likely a mystical system not a language.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13647-manannansun","name":"Manannansun","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-29T22:10:52-07:00","id":1122613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manannansun</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1122389-looking-for-ogam-write-ups-can-anyone-help#post1122389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi everybody, I am looking for some help in tracking down fanmade write-ups of a purview for Ogam. I know it doesn't play an overly large role in Irish myth, but I feel that at least it should be an option for people playing scions of Ogma, Dagda, and Lugh. I feel it should also be available somehow for a Tuatha character who desires to specialize in secret knowledge, mystic endeavors, relic creation, etc. I know it was mentioned in the fiction preview depicting the Dagda's library, but I feel historically that it was more than just a writing system considering the fact it was seeming only used for grave inscriptions, and the like in archeological evidence. Additionally if you recall its mention in myth, Ogma's message to Lugh (warning of an attempt to steal one of his wives) simply consisted of the symbol Beith used four times and not an actual word or sentence. I have studied Irish Reconstructionist Pagan writings on the subject (I personally recommend Erynn Rowan Laurie's &quot;Ogam: Weaving Word Wisdom&quot;) and they indicate it was likely a mystical system not a language.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, Ogham. I love Ogham, not really for it's functionality, it's sort of terrible at it's job. The fact it's not very good at it's job, being an alphabet, is what is so interesting. Lots of work have gone into that, it is sort of adorably cludgy as a development. I think the running theory in academia at the moment is that it is an adaption of the Latin alphabet, sort of like a different set of letters, which is why it is so brutally dodgy for writing in Old Irish. I don't know how popular the 'sign language' theory is (that it could have been put together as a sign language initially since the oldest letters are all limited to five lines, one for each digit on your hand) but it's a personal favorite of mine for Scion. I don't know the current discussion on religious functions of Ogham, but in the Tain it seems to be pretty commonly understood. CuChulain uses it to leave challenges for the invading army by carving it into wood. Just using it as an alphabet to leave a message behind him, no real magical side of it. It's just a set of goading challenges stalling the invading army.<br /> <br /> I can actually explain a bit of the illusion of Ogham though. Ogham gets deeply associated with the Ogham stones, but it's important to remember that lacking of evidence is not evidence of lacking. We don't have any remaining non-stone inscriptions in Ogham, but we <i>do</i> have references to Ogham being inscribed on sticks, and staffs in the early literature. The general idea is that Ogham was probably used both on stone and on wood, but where the stones have stood for two-ish millennium, sticks just didn't survive. I don't know if any were strictly used as burial markers either, but that's a really reasonable misunderstanding. The way the Ogham stones have been explained to me are is that they are like those historic plaques we put up on buildings. &quot;This is where X son of Y died,&quot; or &quot;This is where Y did F and this stone was erected by his grandson H.&quot; I don't know if we have found any bodies underneath the stones though, Iron Age Irish burials are like hen's teeth, the stones are instead death markers, places where people died, but the burial custom appears to be burning since we can't find any corpses.<br /> <br /> But! On the topic of the idea of an Ogham Purview, I think there was a semi-official one done by the company that translated Scion into French, la Bibliotheque Interdite. &quot;Ogham, the Magic of Trees,&quot; I think? They were... a set of alternate Fertility Boons possibly? I never used it, my French is impressively bad. I don't know of any fanmade Purviews just for Ogham though outside of that. If you would like Manannansun, I'm sure the forums here could help you come up with some Boons if you'd like.<br /> <br /> What sort of stuff are you looking for this Purview to be able to do?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","user":"Watcher","date":". 07-30-2017, 01:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-29T23:38:53-07:00","id":1122622,"title":"","content":"I keep being amazed at the breadth of your knowledge Watcher. Burning as a burial custom does make sense, but I hadn't thought of it before. However have you read the legend of Abhartach? in that narrative the dwarf magician who keeps returning from the dead is buried headdown and a thorn tree and large rock are erected on the grave site. But maybe this an exception. I certainly would have burned him, would have saved a lot of work. I actually have Ogam: the Magic of Trees but I was pretty sure there was at least one other version floating around out there. However I can't find it anymore, so I was just wondering if anyone here knew of another version. Anyways thank-you for your help and as always it was a pleasure conversing with you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13647-manannansun","name":"Manannansun","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T12:01:26-07:00","id":1122764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manannansun</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1122389-looking-for-ogam-write-ups-can-anyone-help?p=1122622#post1122622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I keep being amazed at the breadth of your knowledge Watcher. Burning as a burial custom does make sense, but I hadn't thought of it before. However have you read the legend of Abhartach? in that narrative the dwarf magician who keeps returning from the dead is buried headdown and a thorn tree and large rock are erected on the grave site. But maybe this an exception. I certainly would have burned him, would have saved a lot of work. I actually have Ogam: the Magic of Trees but I was pretty sure there was at least one other version floating around out there. However I can't find it anymore, so I was just wondering if anyone here knew of another version. Anyways thank-you for your help and as always it was a pleasure conversing with you.</div> </div> </div> </div>When I was writing that post I was mulling over some of the literary and folkloric mentions of burials I know of. One of the versions of the Tain starts with the Bardic apprentices going by and 'waking up' either Conall Cernach, or Fergus mac Roich to tell the story of the Cattle Raid of Cooley as well. (I can't exactly remember which of those two it was, and all of my books are currently shoved in boxes in preparation for a move) What I would say about Abhartach specifically is that the story was recorded <i>very</i> late, 19th century, so that sort of raises a host of issues. If the story is archaic, it might just be a twist caused by more than a thousand years of Christianity. I have some doubts if the story itself is actually as old as the story claims to be however, I can't get my hands on <i>The Origin and History of Irish Names of Places</i> at the moment, it appears that the Internet Archive is down at the moment oddly, but there are... <i>problems</i> with the mid-late 19th century when it comes to topics like this. Other instances of burial discussed in the Irish Literature tends to be sort of glaringly Christian. Since Christianity has such a major focus on very specific burial practices, I would expect that is where the scant few burials in early Irish literature are from since we can't find any pre-Christian burials except for... I think three Roman burials somewhere? <br /> <br /> I can't remember any other Ogham Boons or Purviews done up, but the rest of the forums might! I know there was a big collection of fan-made stuff on the old forums that got lost when the White Wolf forums closed down. Maybe someone has some pieces around somewhere?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}